; 4513 : // _Can_memcmp_elements<_Elem1, _Elem2> reports whether `_Elem1 == _Elem2` can be optimized to memcmp.
; 4514 : // Here, _Elem1 and _Elem2 aren't top-level const, because we remove_const_t before using _Can_memcmp_elements.
; 4515 : 
; 4516 : // Integral types are eligible for memcmp in very specific cases.
; 4517 : // * They must be the same size. (`int == long` is eligible; `int == long long` isn't.)
; 4518 : // * They can't be volatile.
